@startuml
title C4 code - Repository intelligence - active session capacity
package "Host session" {
  class "SessionStart and PreToolUse hooks" as Hook <<host event>>
  class "record-session-facts" as Record <<command>>
  class "Codex session transcript" as Transcript <<bounded source>>
  class "Codex app-server config/read" as Config <<effective settings>>
  class "Agent request" as Agent <<caller>>
}

package "Prism MCP server" {
  class "HostSessionFactStore" as Store <<module>>
  class "CodexHostAdapter" as Adapter <<module>>
  class "CodexTranscriptMetadata" as TranscriptMetadata <<classifier>>
  class "CodexEffectiveConfig" as EffectiveConfig <<reader>>
  class "resolveActiveSessionCapacity" as Active <<function>>
  class "resolveSessionCapacity" as Resolve <<existing function>>
  class "CapacityRegistry" as Registry <<existing data contract>>
  class "mcp.callRepositoryTool" as Mcp <<existing function>>
}

Hook --> Record : provides session and active model facts
Record --> Adapter : allowlists and normalizes Codex facts
Adapter --> TranscriptMetadata : requests correlated identity
TranscriptMetadata --> Transcript : reads first session_meta and latest bounded token_count
Adapter --> EffectiveConfig : requests effective capacity settings
EffectiveConfig --> Config : reads effective values and layer provenance
Record --> Store : writes one digest-keyed atomic record
Store --> Store : evicts expired and oldest records under quota
Store --> Store : rejects links and uses token-owned retention locks
Record --> Agent : emits key and plugin data directory as context
Agent --> Mcp : supplies key, data directory, and canonical project root
Agent --> Mcp : supplies both active overrides or neither
Mcp --> Active : requests same-session capacity
Active --> Store : reads bounded fresh facts
Active --> Resolve : applies caller, runtime, config, and proven-default precedence
Resolve --> Registry : selects an exact supported profile

note right of Active
  Condition: facts are missing, stale, ambiguous, or cross-session.
  Response: return UNSUPPORTED with a stable reason code.
  Governing requirement: active-session-capacity.md section 3.
end note
@enduml
